  screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1778182927579_2421 { 
 } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-yui_3_17_2_1_17781829275
 79_2421 .sqs-html-content { } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { } T
 here’s nothing as entertaining as hearing folks from the past explain ho
 w things used to be—here guests learn about oyster shell processing on t
 he Petaluma River\, an enterprise that continued for more than a century. 
 Hear stories from people who worked the egg trade\, ran messages between b
 usinesses\, managed boarding houses\, and built enterprises that fueled a 
 growing city. As you move through downtown and along historic riverbanks\,
  you’ll gain a deeper appreciation for the ingenuity\, industrious spiri
 t\, and daily lives that shaped Petaluma—and the river that made it all 
 possible. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment and instruction 
 provided. Just bring your curiosity—and be ready to see Petaluma through
  new eyes. #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1778182927579_4668 { --stroke-style: none\;
 --stroke-thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: initial\; }
